      "content": "Before calling a plumber, you can check the temperature and pressure relief valve to ensure it's set correctly, which can sometimes cause unusual sounds. However, **never** open the tank itself, especially if you suspect an electrical or internal mechanical issue. If T&P valve checks don't reveal an obvious problem, the rhythmic knocking is serious enough to warrant professional inspection.",
